### Spiza API — Rider HTTP Client requests
### Start the app with `docker compose up --build -d`, then replace the API key
### with the value from `docker compose exec -T spiza cat /data/.spiza-api-key`.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:7492
@apiKey = REPLACE_WITH_API_KEY
@barcode = REPLACE_WITH_BARCODE

### Liveness (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Accept: application/json

### Readiness (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready
Accept: application/json

### Search by barcode
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?barcode={{barcode}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Search by text
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products?q=milk&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Current prices in Split and Solin; Kaštela is used per retailer only when both lack a price
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/prices/current?barcode={{barcode}}&city=Split&fallbackAreas=Ka%C5%A1tela
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Batch lookup with the same location rules
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/prices/batch
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "barcodes": ["{{barcode}}", "REPLACE_WITH_ANOTHER_BARCODE"],
  "city": "Split",
  "fallbackAreas": ["Kaštela"]
}

### Local price history
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/prices/history?barcode={{barcode}}&city=Split&fallbackAreas=Ka%C5%A1tela
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Data freshness and coverage
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/coverage
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Export prices as JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/export/prices?format=json&city=Split&fallbackAreas=Ka%C5%A1tela
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json

### Export prices as CSV
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/export/prices?format=csv&city=Split&fallbackAreas=Ka%C5%A1tela
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: text/csv

### Queue a source refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}
Accept: application/json
